(MUHYISSUNNAH DARS UKKUDA - ARABIC GRAMMAR CHART) '
(================================================) '
(Text: Alfiyyah Ibn Malik \(1000 Verses of Arabic Grammar\)) '
() '
(1. AL-KALAM \(Speech and Its Components\):) '
(   - Kalamunafadun Mufidun Kastaqim, Wasmun Wa Fi'lun Thumma Harfun Al-Kalim.) '
(   - Speech consists of Noun \(Ism\), Verb \(Fi'l\), and Particle \(Harf\).) '
() '
(2. SIGNS OF NOUNS \(Al-Ism\):) '
(   - Bil-Jarri Wat-Tanwini Wan-Nida Wa Al, Wa Musnadin Lil-Ismi Tamyizun Hasal.) '
(   - Nouns are recognized by Genitive case \(Jarr\), Tanween, Alif-Lam, and Musnad.) '
() '
(3. SIGNS OF VERBS \(Al-Fi'l\):) '
(   - Bi-Ta Fa'alta Wa Atat Wa Yaf'ali, Wa Nuni Aqbilanna Fi'lun Yanjali.) '
(   - Verbs are recognized by Ta-Fa'alta, Ta-at, and Nun al-Tawkeed.) '
() '
(Prepared for MSA Ukkuda Grammar Course.) '
ET
